MaaFramework
============

Repository: https://github.com/MaaXYZ/MaaFramework
Migration source: commit 0fc6025c2fc224a171b57d89505e8d47acd2a8b1
Project licence: GNU Lesser General Public License version 3.
This extraction follows LGPL-3.0-or-later, as stated in LICENSE; the full
LGPL v3 and GPL v3 texts are both supplied in LICENSE.

src/backends/windows/gdi.rs is a Rust migration of:
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/GdiScreencap.h
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/GdiScreencap.cpp
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/HwndUtils.hpp (window_size/conversion order)

src/backends/windows/print_window.rs is a Rust migration of:
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/PrintWindowScreencap.h
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/PrintWindowScreencap.cpp

src/backends/custom.rs partially migrates the screenshot and connection path of:
  source/MaaCustomControlUnit/Manager/CustomControlUnitMgr.{h,cpp}

It preserves the borrowed callback table/context, synchronous caller execution,
nonzero MaaBool results, false-output preservation and true-empty replacement.
Explicit acceptance extracts unchanged selected manager bodies and the raw
MaaImageBufferSetRawData body from source/Common/MaaBuffer.cpp. It compiles the
real include/MaaFramework/Instance/MaaCustomController.h callback declarations,
Utility/MaaBuffer.h and prepared MaaUtils ImageBuffer implementation/vtable,
linking OpenCV core/imgproc/imgcodecs without stub codec symbols. The selected
body model is not the full manager virtual ABI, create/destroy API, input
implementation or SDK provider. Native source/license inputs accompany each
external acceptance batch; default builds and the custom-only core have no
OpenCV dependency. Full Custom and P1 acceptance remain outstanding.

The explicit OpenCV imgcodecs acceptance build additionally links current
formal libpng (https://libpng.org/pub/png/libpng.html, libpng-2.0 licence) and
zlib (https://zlib.net/, Zlib licence) for actual PNG encode/decode. Each batch
archives their upstream source, exact tag/commit resolution and original
LICENSE texts, plus the native codec probe and build identity. These are
acceptance dependencies; default product/core builds do not link them.

src/platform/windows/pseudo_minimize.rs and
src/backends/windows/print_window_pseudo.rs and frame_pool_pseudo.rs are Rust migrations of:
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/PseudoMinimizeHelper.h
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/PseudoMinimizeHelper.cpp
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/PrintWindowWithPseudoMinimizeScreencap.h
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/FramePoolWithPseudoMinimizeScreencap.h

The helper retains its synchronous pre-capture action, 100ms monitor polling,
original partial-failure behavior, and join-before-restore shutdown order.
It uses standard Arc/atomics with guarded immutable style snapshots, a serial
caller owner, fallible state allocation and fixed-size failure evidence.
Inactive restoration remains distinct from stop's re-minimization. Native
validation uses independently pumped controlled windows; original/Rust layered
and nonlayered capture/stop/inactive/target-loss checks remain separate from
foreground-control availability and unresolved historical parity failures. This
is an incomplete migration component, not a public capture interface.

src/backends/windows/screen_dc.rs is a Rust migration of:
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/ScreenDCScreencap.h
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/ScreenDCScreencap.cpp

src/platform/windows/foreground.rs and geometry.rs migrate the default path of:
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Base/ForegroundUtils.h
  source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Screencap/HwndUtils.hpp

They preserve the unpatched rcWork adjustment, native waits and cross-window
DWORD cooldown. Atomic storage avoids the original unsynchronized shared
DWORD access without serializing the native requests. Checked geometry rejects
undefined integer overflow; the original compatible-mode scale path is pending.

The three GDI-family backends share DC/bitmap cleanup and private conversion/error
types in gdi_resources.rs and gdi_types.rs. PrintWindow retains the original
GetDIBits path, temporarily unselecting its bitmap to satisfy the native API
precondition and reselecting it before the original BGRA2BGR conversion point.
Window GDI and ScreenDC share the original GetBitmapBits readback in gdi_read.rs;
ScreenDC retains null screen-DC ownership and client-origin desktop pixels.

These original files do not contain additional per-file copyright or licence
notices. Their original source identities and licence materials are retained
in the external provenance records. The Rust migration preserves the original
native path and conversion point; it adds checked sizes, bitmap layout/full-read
validation, fallible CPU allocation and separate cleanup error evidence.

src/backends/windows/frame_pool.rs is a partial Rust migration of the fixed
FramePoolScreencap.{h,cpp}. It preserves the hardware swapchain, original Create,
caller execution, polling/cache clone and conversion-before-Unmap. Target-row
copying, checked content/layout and explicit factory owners are documented safety
adaptations; this is not completed FramePool or P1 acceptance.

src/backends/windows/desktop_dup.rs and desktop_dup_window.rs migrate the fixed
DesktopDupScreencap.{h,cpp} and DesktopDupWindowScreencap.{h,cpp}. They preserve
hardware/factory/output selection, warmups, waiting and conversion/crop order.
The original mapped cv::Mat outlives Unmap/ReleaseFrame; the Rust migration
instead copies defined BGRA rows while mapped, retaining the original later
conversion point. Packed window BGR isolation adds another explicit target copy.
These safety adaptations are counted and documented; full native/source parity
and complete backend/P1 acceptance remain outstanding.

src/backends/windows/manager.rs, manager_native.rs and the caller-DPI platform
wrapper partially migrate only the screenshot path of the fixed
source/MaaWin32ControlUnit/Manager/Win32ControlUnitMgr.{h,cpp}, including the
MaaDef.h method values. Input implementations are excluded. Native acceptance
extracts the original screenshot function bodies and enum into its build tree;
an explicit input=None declaration shim and scripted boundaries are not the
complete original control-unit class. It also compiles the selected external
MaaUtils Time.hpp duration_since body; MaaUtils source/licence identities and
all applicable notices accompany the external acceptance inputs. These targets
and OpenCV remain excluded from default product builds.

src/backends/linux/pipewire.rs partially migrates the consumer control flow of
the fixed source/MaaLinuxControlUnit/Screencap/PipeWireScreencap.cpp. Native
setup, POD and stream/buffer handling are not implemented by that module yet.
Explicit portable acceptance extracts the original wait/lock helpers, format
table and consumer methods into its external build tree, with fake loop/clock
and symbolic format IDs plus real OpenCV Mat ownership/conversion. This is not
the complete original Linux class or native PipeWire acceptance. The oracle
and OpenCV stay outside the default product dependency tree.

The explicit tests/upstream-parity/linux-pipewire source context compiles the
fixed complete PipeWireScreencap header/source externally, with an exact extracted
screenshot base declaration and explicit private namespace/logging overlays.
Input/ConfigBase and the rest of the framework are excluded. Native PipeWire/SPA,
DRM declarations and OpenCV remain real; their source/license inputs are archived
with that diagnostic batch. This target is not a native Rust capture backend or
part of default product builds and SDK assets.

src/backends/linux/wlr.rs partially migrates the fixed:
  source/MaaLinuxControlUnit/Screencap/WlrScreencap.{h,cpp}
  source/MaaLinuxControlUnit/Wayland/WaylandClient.{h,cpp}
  source/MaaLinuxControlUnit/Wayland/WaylandHelper.{h,cpp}
  source/MaaLinuxControlUnit/Base/MemfdBuffer.{h,cpp}

The private capture slice preserves callback-internal recursive waiting and
frame ownership through caller conversion. Checked layouts/version/path, RAII
and an added independent CPU copy are documented safety adaptations. Shared
client, full native error/format and remaining P1 parity are incomplete. The
platform channel uses maintained bindings and an original one-function C
adapter for the native queue getter missing from wayland-sys.

The explicit tests/upstream-parity/linux-wlr source context compiles those
fixed upstream files and original generated C protocols unchanged, with an
extracted screenshot base and explicit private namespace/logging overlays.
An external kernel-random name provider is separate from the original UUID
utility. Its passive input-manager fixture creates no host input device or
action. Real OpenCV conversion acceptance reuses the self-owned private
linux-pipewire adapter without a PipeWire runtime dependency. These acceptance
targets and reference inputs remain outside default builds and SDK assets;
their native/source licence materials are archived externally per batch.

The separate self-owned Wlr protocol fixture uses the real libwayland-server
IPC/SHM helper and generated server declarations from the prepared latest formal
wlroots protocol XML. XML, generated files, corresponding source and original
copyright/MIT notices are archived with each explicit native batch. The source
client still compiles the fixed original generated protocols independently.
This fixture is not a compositor, input provider or product backend; it compares
original/Rust six-format bytes, including the original packed-step/YInvert
limitations. RGB888 acceptance executes a real OpenCV copyTo; the preceding
Rust independent CPU copy is an additional documented safety cost.

The explicit tests/upstream-parity/macos-screencap context compiles the fixed
source/MaaMacOSControlUnit/Screencap/ScreenCaptureKitScreencap.{h,mm}
unchanged, including its sample-buffer conversion. Its screenshot base is
extracted from the same fixed Base/UnitBase.h; private namespace/logging exclude
unrelated input/framework code. Original Objective-C manual reference counting,
callback conversion and native waiting stay in that source. Self-owned AppKit
fixtures and OpenCV acceptance preparation are separate; no Rust macOS product
migration or completed P1 is claimed. Native inputs and their applicable notices
remain external, and this target is excluded from default builds and SDK assets.

src/backends/macos/screen_capture_kit.rs and the private platform pixel-buffer
owner now begin Rust migration of that same fixed ScreenCaptureKitScreencap
source, using maintained objc2/block2/dispatch2 bindings. Native semaphore
waiting, callback conversion and source create-reference retention remain U;
explicit test-only residual reclamation is separate from product cleanup.
Checked layout/locking, a counted independent CPU copy and contained failures
are documented safety adaptations. Same-window original/native Rust probes
and C++ CPU Mat ownership tests are not full macOS/P1 acceptance or public SDK
bindings. The shared OpenCV acceptance source remains outside the core tree.

src/backends/macos/manager.rs and manager_native.rs migrate the screenshot-only
MacOSControlUnitMgr path: connection/owner replacement, result forwarding,
decimal UUID and inactive semantics. Input=None is an explicit acceptance
boundary. The private native targets extract six unchanged manager function
bodies; their original identities, source/license materials and scripted/native
scope accompany the external batch. Metadata/full manager/API acceptance is
pending; no public SDK binding or new input functionality is provided.

Microsoft C++/WinRT
=================

Repository: https://github.com/microsoft/cppwinrt
src/platform/windows/wgc_factory.rs adapts the activation-loader algorithm from
the selected Windows SDK C++/WinRT winrt/base.h; wgc.rs adapts its completion
event wait from winrt/Windows.Foundation.h. The original Microsoft copyright
and MIT notice are preserved in that source and licenses/cppwinrt-MIT.txt; the
Rust adaptation is also subject to the project's LGPL-3.0-or-later terms.
The exact SDK/header identity is archived with FramePool validation inputs.

The explicit native acceptance targets compile original MaaFramework and
MaaUtils sources and link OpenCV/Boost from external preparation inputs. Their
applicable licence/notice materials accompany those acceptance artifacts.
The separate upstream-context frame-pool diagnostic additionally compiles the
original FramePoolScreencap.{h,cpp} in an isolated executable. It observes caller
COM/runtime state and source pixels; it is not a Rust FramePool migration.
They are excluded from default product builds. This file is not the completed
asset-specific distribution notice inventory, which is verified in P5.

meojson
--------

The explicit manager-metadata model additionally compiles the fixed Windows
and macOS manager get_info bodies with their copied metadata member declarations
and real MaaDef/meojson types. Input=None is an explicit query boundary; native
manager constructors, virtual ABI and capture are excluded. The same private
Rust managers now produce the corresponding field/selector views using std,
without a JSON library or reference material in default product dependencies.

Repository: https://github.com/MistEO/meojson
The explicit Linux configuration source oracle uses the latest formal meojson
headers, archived with their original source and licence per batch. The private
Rust manager_config reader adapts its observed byte/string, number, duplicate
key and document-boundary semantics, without a C++ or meojson runtime dependency.
The observed parser trait and dependency identity are verified by the explicit
reference target. These legacy semantics are not a new SDK JSON contract.

